<Project Sdk="Microsoft.NET.Sdk">
	<PropertyGroup>
		<TargetFrameworks>net8.0;net9.0;net10.0</TargetFrameworks>
		<GeneratePackageOnBuild>false</GeneratePackageOnBuild>
		<PackageId>TA.DataAccess.SqlServer</PackageId>
		<Version>2.4.0</Version>
		<Authors>Touhid Alam</Authors>
		<Company>Touhid Alam</Company>
		<Product>TA.DataAccess.SqlServer</Product>
		<Description>TA.DataAccess.SqlServer is a comprehensive .NET library designed to simplify database operations with SQL Server. It provides a range of methods to execute queries, retrieve data, and perform CRUD operations using strongly-typed models.</Description>
		<PackageTags>SQLServer DataAccess CRUD Database ORM execute queries retrieve data insert update delete models</PackageTags>
		<RepositoryUrl>https://github.com/touhidalam69/DataAccess_SqlServer</RepositoryUrl>
		<RepositoryType>git</RepositoryType>
		<PackageReadmeFile>README.md</PackageReadmeFile>
		<PackageLicenseFile>LICENSE</PackageLicenseFile>
		<Title>DataAccess.SqlServer</Title>
		<Copyright>MIT</Copyright>
		<PackageProjectUrl>https://touhidalam.com/simplifying-sql-server-database-operations-for-net-developers/</PackageProjectUrl>
		<PackageReleaseNotes>2.4.0: New - ISqlServerOperations: one interface holding every data operation. ISqlServerHelper (adds BeginTransaction) and ISqlServerUnitOfWork (adds Commit/Rollback) extend it, so repository code written against it runs inside or outside a transaction; both still declare their existing members, so assemblies built against 2.3 keep working. DeleteModel&lt;T&gt;(model) (+ async) deletes by every key column of the model and, with [RowVersion], only if the version still matches - otherwise DBConcurrencyException, as for UpdateModel. InsertModel/InsertModelAsync also write back [Computed] columns (database defaults, computed columns, values set by insert triggers), re-read from the new row in the same round trip when it can be found by its [Identity] or by [Key] values the model supplies; the [RowVersion] written back is then the version after insert triggers ran. Behavior change: after InsertModel, [Computed] properties hold the stored values instead of what the object had. 2.3.1: Security - depends on patched System.Security.Cryptography.Pkcs (8.0.2 / 9.0.22 / 10.0.14) instead of the vulnerable 8.0.1 / 9.0.4 brought in by Microsoft.Data.SqlClient 6.0.2 (CVE-2026-84008 high, CVE-2026-70162 moderate). Packaging - built and published by CI from the release tag, so Source Link points at the released commit (the 2.3.0 package on nuget.org pointed at the 2.2.0 commit); Microsoft.SourceLink.GitHub 10.0.403 (build-time only). No API or behavior changes from 2.3.0. 2.3.0: Fixes - InsertModel works on tables with triggers (identity returned via OUTPUT ... INTO instead of a bare OUTPUT, which SQL Server rejects with error 334); composite keys: UpdateModel, GetModelByKey, DeleteByKey and Exists use every [Key] column (pass an object[] of key values) - a single value for a composite key is now rejected instead of matching on the first key column only, which could update or delete several rows. New - [RowVersion] optimistic concurrency (UpdateModel checks the version, throws DBConcurrencyException on conflict, writes the new version back; InsertModel writes it back too); [Computed] for database-filled columns (read, never written); [InsertOnly] for columns never updated (CreatedAt/CreatedBy); [Key(Order = n)] for composite key order; SelectMultiple/SelectMultipleInterpolated (+ async) for 2 or 3 result sets in one round trip; SqlServerHelperOptions.UseDateTime2 to send DateTime as datetime2 (default off, unchanged behavior). Packaging - 2.2.0's net8.0/net9.0 assemblies were stale builds without the 2.2.0 API; this package is built for all targets. Note: ISqlServerHelper and ISqlServerUnitOfWork gained members (source-breaking for custom implementers only). 2.2.0 (additive): interpolated read API - SelectInterpolated&lt;T&gt;/SelectInterpolated (DataTable)/SelectStreamInterpolatedAsync&lt;T&gt; (+ async), completing the FormattableString surface for queries. 2.1.0 (additive): transactions/unit-of-work (BeginTransaction/BeginTransactionAsync -&gt; ISqlServerUnitOfWork); stored procedures (ExecuteProcedure/QueryProcedure/ExecuteProcedureScalar); ExecuteScalar&lt;T&gt;; InsertModel now writes back the generated [Identity] value; Count/Exists; attribute-resolved GetModelByKey/DeleteByKey; SelectPaged (OFFSET/FETCH); batch ExecuteInterpolated. Performance: per-column compiled coercion delegates, await using async disposal, explicit string/Guid/bool parameter typing, streamed bulk insert (no DataTable) + IEnumerable overload. Note: ISqlServerHelper gained members (source-breaking for custom implementers only).</PackageReleaseNotes>
		<PackageIcon>TA.DataAccess.SqlServer.png</PackageIcon>
		<PackAsTool>False</PackAsTool>
		<IsTrimmable>true</IsTrimmable>
		<IsAotCompatible>false</IsAotCompatible>
		<EnableTrimAnalyzer>true</EnableTrimAnalyzer>
		<PublishRepositoryUrl>true</PublishRepositoryUrl>
		<EmbedUntrackedSources>true</EmbedUntrackedSources>
		<IncludeSymbols>true</IncludeSymbols>
		<SymbolPackageFormat>snupkg</SymbolPackageFormat>
		<DebugType>portable</DebugType>
		<DebugSymbols>true</DebugSymbols>
	</PropertyGroup>
	<ItemGroup>
		<None Include="..\..\LICENSE">
			<Pack>True</Pack>
			<PackagePath>\</PackagePath>
		</None>
		<None Include="..\..\README.md">
			<Pack>True</Pack>
			<PackagePath>\</PackagePath>
		</None>
		<None Include="..\..\TA.DataAccess.SqlServer.png">
			<Pack>True</Pack>
			<PackagePath>\</PackagePath>
		</None>
	</ItemGroup>
	<ItemGroup>
		<InternalsVisibleTo Include="TA.DataAccess.SqlServer.Tests" />
	</ItemGroup>
	<ItemGroup>
		<PackageReference Include="Microsoft.Data.SqlClient" Version="6.0.2" />
		<PackageReference Include="Microsoft.Extensions.Configuration.Abstractions" Version="8.0.0" />
		<PackageReference Include="Microsoft.Extensions.Configuration.Binder" Version="8.0.2" />
		<PackageReference Include="Microsoft.Extensions.Logging.Abstractions" Version="9.0.4" />
		<PackageReference Include="Microsoft.SourceLink.GitHub" Version="10.0.403" PrivateAssets="all" />
	</ItemGroup>
	<!--
		Microsoft.Data.SqlClient 6.0.2 brings in System.Security.Cryptography.Pkcs 8.0.1 / 9.0.4, which have
		known vulnerabilities (CVE-2026-84008, CVE-2026-70162). Pin the patched versions so consumers get them.
		Remove once Microsoft.Data.SqlClient depends on patched versions itself.
	-->
	<ItemGroup Condition="'$(TargetFramework)' == 'net8.0'">
		<PackageReference Include="System.Security.Cryptography.Pkcs" Version="8.0.2" />
	</ItemGroup>
	<ItemGroup Condition="'$(TargetFramework)' == 'net9.0'">
		<PackageReference Include="System.Security.Cryptography.Pkcs" Version="9.0.22" />
	</ItemGroup>
	<ItemGroup Condition="'$(TargetFramework)' == 'net10.0'">
		<PackageReference Include="System.Security.Cryptography.Pkcs" Version="10.0.14" />
	</ItemGroup>
</Project>
